# Mac settings checks (advisory — mismatches WARN, not MISS).
# Format: label|kind|location|key|expected[|compare]
# kind: json-editor (cursor or code), defaults, sound-menu-bar-always,
#       machine-name-not-default, next-window-switch-key, chrome-json
# location: editor id, "global" for NSGlobalDomain, Chrome profile dir
#           name (e.g. Default), profile display name (e.g. natera.com),
#           "*" / "@last" for Chrome's last-used profile, or "@all" for every
#           Chrome user profile
# compare: eq (default), at_most (numeric actual <= expected)
# In an interactive terminal gar offers to fix WARNs for json-editor,
# defaults, sound-menu-bar-always, next-window-switch-key, and chrome-json
# kinds. machine-name-not-default is advisory only.
# next-window-switch-key only applies when Karabiner Elements is installed
# and the Czech-QWERTY input source is enabled; it checks that "Move focus to
# next window" (symbolic hotkey 27) is Command-< (ASCII 92, keycode 50) — the
# expected binding on this layout. toggle-switch-key also toggles Command-`,
# but that is not the desired state for this check. The fix writes (92, 50,
# 1048576).
# chrome-json reads Preferences / Secure Preferences under
# ~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome; skipped if Chrome is not
# installed. Startup prefs are per profile — "*" checks the last-used one
# (the profile you pick in "Who's using Chrome?"). session.restore_on_startup=1
# is "Continue where you left off".
Cursor auto-save|json-editor|cursor|files.autoSave|onFocusChange
VS Code auto-save|json-editor|code|files.autoSave|onFocusChange
Keyboard repeat speed|defaults|global|KeyRepeat|2|at_most
Keyboard repeat delay|defaults|global|InitialKeyRepeat|15|at_most
Show all filename extensions|defaults|global|AppleShowAllExtensions|1
Always show volume in menu bar|sound-menu-bar-always||||
Machine name|machine-name-not-default||||
Move focus to next window (Command-<)|next-window-switch-key||||
Chrome On startup: continue where you left off|chrome-json|*|session.restore_on_startup|1
